## What Makes September Nails Different From Regular Fall Nails

Yes, September counts as a fall month for nail purposes, but it is the softest possible version of one. A true fall manicure commits fully to depth and drama. A <strong>September nails</strong> look holds onto restraint, warmth, and a little bit of leftover summer glow, which is exactly why the same burgundy that looks perfect in November can feel heavy-handed on the first of the month. For the full picture of how the back half of the month earns that deeper, no-apologies mood, <a href='/blog/september/late-september-nails'>late september nail ideas</a> covers the complete shift, full fall energy included.

